sdwdate obtains HTTP Date headers through Tor onion services, selecting
independent sources from three upstream pools. It checks the Tor consensus,
uses the median clock offset and retries at randomized intervals.

This OpenBSD adaptation runs the network code as _sdwdate, with a small C
parent handling bounded clock corrections over an inherited private socket.
Tor control authentication requires administrator configuration. Do not run
sdwdate and ntpd concurrently. See the package README before enabling it.
